Side: server.
Sets the exhaustion as it is (Paper's `HumanEntity#setExhaustion`;
vanilla's `FoodData` only adds to it).

Queue `value` to `player` through [`PlayerRef::send_payload`], with its results, after
checking the token: `StaleToken` for one the registrar did not hand out for this type.

A serverbound token has no `send` to a player, so the wrong direction does not compile:
```compile_fail
# use mod_api::*;
fn wrong(token: &ToServer<VarInt>, host: &mut dyn ServerHost, player: PlayerRef) {
    let _ = token.send(host, player, &VarInt(7));
}
```

Stored damage, or zero when no numeric damage override is present.
A plain stack inherits its item's default. Some(0) is an explicit present zero;
[`Self::clear_damage`] records removal of the default component instead.

functions.doc:
`FluidUtil.interactWithFluidHandler` for a block: `player`'s `hand` against the tanks of the
block at `pos` in `level` as `side` reaches them ([`FLUIDS`]), as
[`interact_with_handler`] does. False where the block has no tanks.

A tank block calls it from its `use_item_on` part and answers a success when it is true:

```no_run
use mod_api::{BlockPart, Direction, InteractionResult, ServerHost, UseItemOnEvent, fluid_util};
struct Tank;
#[mod_api::horizon_part]
impl BlockPart for Tank {
    fn use_item_on(
        &self,
        host: &mut dyn ServerHost,
        event: &mut UseItemOnEvent<'_>,
    ) -> Option<InteractionResult> {
        let click = event.click;
        let player = host.player(click.player)?;
        let level = player.level(host)?;
        let side = Direction::ALL.into_iter().find(|d| d.normal() == click.hit.face);
        fluid_util::interact_with_fluid_handler(host, player, click.hand, level, click.pos, side)
            .then_some(InteractionResult::Success)
    }
}
```

`EditBox.getWordPosition(dir, from)`: the character index `dir` words away
from `from`. Forward, past the rest of the word and its spaces; backward,
over any spaces to the start of the word.

macros.doc:
Mark a part implementation and derive the scoped hooks it overrides.

Hook methods must be written explicitly, not generated inside the impl:

```compile_fail
use horizon_mod_api_macros::horizon_part;
trait BlockPart { fn tick(&self) {} }
struct Block;
macro_rules! hook { () => { fn tick(&self) {} }; }
#[horizon_part]
impl BlockPart for Block { hook!(); }
```

fields.doc:
The stored grant date, or `None` when this criterion is not obtained.
Dates use the advancement save format (`yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss Z`);
capturing progress preserves the original date rather than reading a clock.

The block's or mob's own loot table (`minecraft:blocks/stone`, `minecraft:entities/zombie`);
empty when none rolled: the block or mob has none, the `mob_drops` rule is off, a baby
animal. A mob's drops may hold more: a charged creeper's head, a fox's mouth item.

types.doc:
One player's open menu, invalidated on close, replacement or reconnect.
Client menu handles are also invalidated on respawn.

Clicks require a mutable client host, not a server or a read-only hook:
```compile_fail
use mod_api::{MenuRef, ServerHost};
fn wrong(menu: MenuRef, host: &mut dyn ServerHost) {
    menu.click(host, &[]);
}
```
```compile_fail
use mod_api::{MenuRef, ClientHost};
fn wrong(menu: MenuRef, host: &dyn ClientHost) {
    menu.click(host, &[]);
}
```

